SCST: hand a PR registrant to the new session of an I_T nexus when that session is created.

A persistent-reservation registration belongs to the I_T nexus, which iSCSI names by initiator
name and ISID; SPC keeps it across the loss of the nexus and the session's reinstatement. When an
initiator logs in again with the same ISID after iscsi-scst has already freed the old session in
user space, the login is a new session, and scst_pr_init_tgt_dev() left the registrant on the old
session's per-device state (it only assigns a registrant that no tgt_dev holds). The registrant
moved only when the old tgt_dev was freed (scst_pr_clear_tgt_dev()), asynchronously, so for the
6-14 ms between the new session's creation and that free every command of the registered nexus
was refused RESERVATION CONFLICT (measured on the MXFS lab target, 2026-10-23: the five refused
writes of a 4 s path cut all fell inside that window).

Two sessions with one initiator name, ISID and relative target port cannot both be current (a
login with the same ISID reinstates the earlier session), so the new tgt_dev takes the registrant
under the PR write lock; the old tgt_dev's later clear then finds none to hand over.

Not applied. Applying it means rebuilding SCST's modules and reloading them on the lab host,
which takes every target's LUNs away from the lab VMs while it runs: the owner's decision.

--- a/scst/src/scst_pres.c
+++ b/scst/src/scst_pres.c
@@ -1191,12 +1191,25 @@ int scst_pr_init_tgt_dev(struct scst_tgt_dev *tgt_dev)
 	scst_pr_write_lock(dev);

 	reg = scst_pr_find_reg(dev, transport_id, rel_tgt_id);
-	if (reg && !reg->tgt_dev) {
+	if (reg && reg->tgt_dev && reg->tgt_dev != tgt_dev) {
+		/*
+		 * The registrant is still linked to the per-device state of an
+		 * earlier session of the same I_T nexus, which is being freed.
+		 * The new session is the nexus now: take the registrant, so its
+		 * commands are not refused until the old state is gone.
+		 */
+		TRACE_PR("Moving reg %s/%d (%p) from tgt_dev %p to new tgt_dev %p (dev %s)",
+			 debug_transport_id_to_initiator_name(transport_id),
+			 rel_tgt_id, reg, reg->tgt_dev, tgt_dev, dev->virt_name);
+		reg->tgt_dev->registrant = NULL;
+		tgt_dev->registrant = reg;
+		reg->tgt_dev = tgt_dev;
+	} else if (reg && !reg->tgt_dev) {
 		TRACE_PR("Assigning reg %s/%d (%p) to tgt_dev %p (dev %s)",
 			 debug_transport_id_to_initiator_name(transport_id),
 			 rel_tgt_id, reg, tgt_dev, dev->virt_name);
 		tgt_dev->registrant = reg;
 		reg->tgt_dev = tgt_dev;
 	}

 	scst_pr_write_unlock(dev);
